<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Breaking news from AFRICA, Maghreb and Sub-Saharan Africa - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of events, politics and social issues across Africa, including North Africa (the Maghreb) and the Sahel, aided by our network of correspondents and experts across the continent.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:52:02 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Perspective</category><title>Ethiopia-Eritrea: Is there a risk of a wider conflict?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261022-ethiopia-eritrea-is-there-a-risk-of-a-wider-conflict</link><description>
Concerns are mounting as Ethiopia and Eritrea inch closer to war. With Ethiopia now having taken control of the border town of Zalambessa, the fear is that Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed will send his troops into Eritrea. In Perspective, we spoke to Martin Plaut, a senior research fellow at the Institute of Commonwealth Studies at the University of London.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a98b6ee-ce19-11f1-8fb6-97baf3e9dd31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6186ba6e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a98b6ee-ce19-11f1-8fb6-97baf3e9dd31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6186ba6e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ffa2408c-cdf2-11f1-9d41-53ef36ae02a5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:40:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yinka OYETADE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Cameroon: Ten years after a massive train disaster, victims are still awaiting justice</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-cameroon-ten-years-after-a-massive-train-disaster-victims-are-still-awaiting-justice</link><description>
It has been ten years since a Cameroon National Railway Intercity train travelling between Yaounde and Douala derailed and became the country's worst ever railway disaster. Seventy-nine people were killed and hundreds were injured.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/319a19c0-cd76-11f1-be77-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/AP16296707809075.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/319a19c0-cd76-11f1-be77-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/AP16296707809075.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f2e40f5c-ce1e-11f1-a178-c9372df3da2e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:23:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Sudan's war escalates as UN warns of wider regional crisis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261021-sudan-s-war-escalates-as-un-warns-of-wider-regional-crisis</link><description>
In tonight's edition: Sudan's brutal war continues to take a devastating regional toll, as a drone strike in Abyei reportedly kills 153 people. We speak to the UN envoy for Sudan following an emergency international meeting on the escalating crisis. Also, health authorities prepare to coordinate a response as Ebola cases emerge in Nigeria and rise in Kenya. Finally, 10 years after Cameroon’s deadliest railway disaster, families of the 79 victims are still fighting for justice, saying their pain has yet to be acknowledged.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25d330b6-cda0-11f1-942a-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3969bf04.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25d330b6-cda0-11f1-942a-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3969bf04.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cc368094-cd9f-11f1-9510-3b56e5302474</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:41:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Neither the Sudanese military, nor the RSF take any acknowledgement of human life in this war'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/neither-the-sudanese-military-nor-the-rsf-take-any-acknowledgement-of-human-life-in-this-war</link><description>
The death toll from a drone strike Monday on a market in an area disputed between Sudan and South Sudan has risen to 153 and is likely even higher, a local official told AFP on Wednesday. Authorities in Abyei district said the strike on the Amiet market involved the use of multiple munitions and was carried out by the Sudanese army. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Jan Pospisil, Sudan Affairs Analyst at the Peace and Conflict Resolution Evidence Platform. He says that for a long time the Sudanese army has tried "to portray a picture internationally that they are humane, whereas RSF is committing atrocities. Here we see very clearly that there is not much difference between these two".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/303326fa-cd83-11f1-989f-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-203844-205016-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/303326fa-cd83-11f1-989f-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-203844-205016-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3521d5da-cd83-11f1-ac98-f9a30321d3f0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:28:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kenya: Trial shows crucial role of religion in Shakahola massacre</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-kenya-trial-shows-crucial-role-of-religion-in-shakahola-massacre</link><description>
The Kenyan cult leader found guilty on Monday of the deaths of 190 children and one adult will be sentenced on November 6th. Paul Mackenzie starved his followers in what became known as the Shakahola massacre. But this trial was about more than just a criminal and his accomplices. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Bastien Renouil.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb376dba-cc01-11f1-9791-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292477298169.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb376dba-cc01-11f1-9791-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292477298169.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">07f9b834-cd51-11f1-8c08-29ca1ae5660b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:48:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>South African former police chief accused of sex trafficking denied bail</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-south-african-former-police-chief-accused-of-sex-trafficking-denied-bail</link><description>
South Africa's former deputy national commissioner, Shadrack Sibiya, has been denied bail. He is facing charges of rape, trafficking and is accused of sexually grooming a child. Investigators had argued that his accusers would be in danger if he was let out. FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3f272878-cd51-11f1-844d-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7cd460dc.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3f272878-cd51-11f1-844d-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7cd460dc.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">18493d92-cd4f-11f1-b3a0-1773a65f3b01</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:44:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nigeria records its first Ebola case amid rapid regional spread</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-amid-rapid-regional-spread</link><description>
After Kenya and Uganda, Nigeria has now announced its first Ebola case – a woman who was admitted to a private hospital in Abuja and travelled from Uganda. The outbreak, which originated in DR Congo in May, has been described by health officials as ​thefastest-spreading on record. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Sam Olukoya.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/48a63b76-cd53-11f1-9c1d-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T045618Z-1772179031-RC2G4OAZODI8-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-NIGERIA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/48a63b76-cd53-11f1-9c1d-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T045618Z-1772179031-RC2G4OAZODI8-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-NIGERIA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">da5056e4-cd4c-11f1-b5cb-6968c0ef0e51</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:28:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>US sanctions on ICC are 'a shock' and 'unacceptable', Nobel peace laureate Navi Pillay says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261021-us-sanctions-on-icc-are-a-shock-and-unacceptable-nobel-peace-laureate-navi-pillay-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Nobel Peace Prize laureate Navi Pillay described the US sanctions imposed on the International Criminal Court (ICC) hours after her award as "a shock" and "unacceptable". The South African judge also defended the UN commission of inquiry she chaired which concluded that Israel had committed genocide in Gaza: "We didn't come to that conclusion lightly." Rejecting claims that the ICC targets Africa, she said "the court is not selective".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/36f02c16-cd30-11f1-bde0-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/Untitled-Sequence-01-26.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/36f02c16-cd30-11f1-bde0-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/Untitled-Sequence-01-26.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">38559cb0-cd32-11f1-998a-0996ab77a850</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:11:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Nigeria records first Ebola case as outbreak spreads across Africa</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261020-nigeria-records-first-ebola-case-as-outbreak-spreads-across-africa</link><description>
Nigeria has confirmed its first Ebola case in Africa's latest outbreak, while Kenya reported its ninth infection, raising fears of further spread across the continent. Africa CDC chief Jean Kaseya warned of an “extremely serious threat” and urged the international community to send funding, medical supplies and health workers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db9f009a-cccf-11f1-8fb9-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26293670227514.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db9f009a-cccf-11f1-8fb9-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26293670227514.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a126bcb6-ccdc-11f1-a98c-278e4208fe9c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:18:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db9f009a-cccf-11f1-8fb9-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26293670227514.jpg">© Chinedu Asadu, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Nigeria confirms first Ebola case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nigeria-confirms-first-ebola-case</link><description>
In tonight's programme: Nigeria confirms its first Ebola case in the midst of an outbreak that began in DR Congo in mid-May. Also, a former top South African police officer facing sexual grooming and rape charges is denied bail. Finally, São Tomé and Príncipe's rich volcanic soils produce vanilla pods with an entrancing taste unlike those grown anywhere else.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d169c3e2-cccc-11f1-897d-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0eb05e6c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d169c3e2-cccc-11f1-897d-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0eb05e6c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9922808c-cccc-11f1-8628-cd2ba0c8870d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:28:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>More than 150 killed in Sudan drone strike on disputed Abyei border region</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261020-more-than-150-killed-sudan-drone-strike-disputed-abyei-border-region</link><description>
At least 153 people have been killed in a drone strike on a market in the disputed Abyei region, where a fire at a nearby fuel depot continued to burn on Tuesday. Local officials blamed Sudan’s military for Monday’s attack, which also left dozens injured. 
 

 

 

</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06f56856-cc9e-11f1-acba-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP071212050372.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06f56856-cc9e-11f1-acba-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP071212050372.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">46b3841a-cc9d-11f1-88ca-6b9c4a17bd3c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:24:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06f56856-cc9e-11f1-acba-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP071212050372.jpg">© Alfred de Montesquiou, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ivorian DJ digs forgotten tracks, on the hunt for great classics</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-ivorian-dj-digs-forgotten-tracks-on-the-hunt-for-great-classics</link><description>
Cédric Kouamé travels across Ivory Coast to collect old vinyl records before restoring them. The Ivorian DJ hopes to bring national attention to his passion through an official centre dedicated to the country's historical archives, as FRANCE 24's team on the ground reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e84694e-cc82-11f1-9ed1-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-40128c7c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e84694e-cc82-11f1-9ed1-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-40128c7c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">47159f18-cc81-11f1-a7d9-1be4b0761cb5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:09:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Exiled critic of Rwandan President Kagame found beheaded in Uganda</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-exiled-critic-of-rwandan-president-kagame-found-beheaded-in-uganda</link><description>
Robert Kabera, a former Rwandan soldier living in Uganda, where he had become a vocal critic of his government back home, was found decapitated near Kampala. Rwandan authorities have been accused of assassinating opponents of President Paul Kagame. FRANCE 24's Aurore Bayoud reports from Kigali, Rwanda.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74318ee8-cc82-11f1-a8e7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5355095f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74318ee8-cc82-11f1-a8e7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5355095f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">12942f5a-cc74-11f1-bba5-fd42895681a0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:34:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Niger, Mali and Burkina Faso resume dialogue with ECOWAS regional bloc</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-niger-mali-and-burkina-faso-resume-dialogue-with-ecowas-regional-bloc</link><description>
Three junta-ruled Sahel states – Niger, Mali and Burkina Faso – on Saturday resumed dialogue with the ECOWAS regional bloc, which they withdrew from more than 18 months ago. They agreed to work towards a “framework agreement” on cooperation. FRANCE 24’s regional correspondent Harold Girard tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0dee99ea-cc7e-11f1-9a40-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7a2f75c4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0dee99ea-cc7e-11f1-9a40-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7a2f75c4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bfc4b450-cc75-11f1-94e7-630410e1b9e5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:21:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Kenyan cult leader found guilty of murder</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261020-kenyan-cult-leader-found-guilty-of-murder</link><description>
In tonight's programme: Kenyan cult leader Paul Mackenzie is convicted of 191 murders, 190 of which were of children. Also, a former Rwandan soldier and outspoken government critic, Robert Kabera, is found decapitated in Uganda. Plus we meet a young Ivorian music lover who travels around the country looking for old-school sounds that need a little TLC. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f871ee72-cc7e-11f1-bb25-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0ac0abc7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f871ee72-cc7e-11f1-bb25-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0ac0abc7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6fe7542c-cc04-11f1-94b4-e9ecffe55742</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:15:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Drone attacks kill scores in Sudan's West Kordofan state and capital Khartoum</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261019-drone-attack-near-southern-sudan-market-kills-scores</link><description>At least 80 people were killed in a drone strike near a market in Sudan’s southern West Kordofan state, a medical source and a witness said Monday, in one of the deadliest single attacks since the Sudan war erupted in 2023. A separate drone attack Monday in the capital Khartoum killed four, including three children.</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fc4ffbc-8edb-11f1-8f3b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8TT6ZQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fc4ffbc-8edb-11f1-8f3b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8TT6ZQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bd633ea0-cbbe-11f1-836a-2b4eb9c3e037</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:00:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fc4ffbc-8edb-11f1-8f3b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8TT6ZQ.jpg">© Ebrahim Hamid, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Kenya confirms third Ebola case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-confirms-third-ebola-case</link><description>
In tonight's programme: Kenya confirms a third case of Ebola, a relative of a man who died earlier this month after travelling from DR Congo. Also, Cameroonian journalist Ambe Macmillan is recovering in hospital after being shot in the legs by gunmen in Bamenda. Finally, we meet Ghanaian artist Ibrahim Mahama, who digs deep into his country's colonial and industrial past to lay new creative foundations for generations to come.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a8234156-c99e-11f1-ac97-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d9ec4c85.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a8234156-c99e-11f1-ac97-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d9ec4c85.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">10ae7b4c-c99e-11f1-8421-dfc1b0a04897</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:25:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>James MULHOLLAND</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ethiopia announces interim government in Tigray, aims for polls in six months</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261016-ethiopia-announces-interim-government-tigray-calls-for-polls-six-months</link><description>
Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed on Friday announced the appointment of an interim administration to prepare elections in the northern Tigray region previously controlled by the Tigray People's Liberation Front that has clashed with government forces since September. The recent conflict revived a war that killed hundreds of thousands between 2020 and 2022.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3f160318-c95f-11f1-8341-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26284531962755.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3f160318-c95f-11f1-8341-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26284531962755.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a670ee4-c95c-11f1-9fa5-c16b5c3a9206</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:05:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3f160318-c95f-11f1-8341-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26284531962755.jpg">© Filmon Equar Hailu, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Kinshasa braces for potential conflict as Kabila joins M23</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/kinshasa-braces-for-potential-conflict-as-kabila-joins-m23</link><description>
In tonight's edition: As former Congolese president Joseph Kabila returns to centre stage with a new alliance with the M23 rebels, political leaders in DR Congo are having to choose sides. Also, the US is calling for restraint in Ethiopia as a rights group warns that the conflict in Tigray is already taking a toll on civilians. And as the season of art fairs returns, we take a look at the rising international visibility of African contemporary art.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ff8b32b4-c8d6-11f1-9f0a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1f4d956c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ff8b32b4-c8d6-11f1-9f0a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1f4d956c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e9081a0c-c8d6-11f1-a367-157581ab610c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:29:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clarisse FORTUNÉ</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Kenya reports second Ebola case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-reports-second-ebola-case</link><description>
In tonight's edition: Kenya confirms a second case of Ebola. Also, Nobel Peace Prize winner Navi Pillay warns that international justice is facing growing pressure. Plus millions of people in Nigeria have been without TikTok for about a month. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9cdc9d84-c876-11f1-ab86-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-ab616c41.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9cdc9d84-c876-11f1-ab86-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-ab616c41.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">17d8f3a2-c80e-11f1-85f9-c588d397f795</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:32:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clarisse FORTUNÉ</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>DR Congo's Kabila launches new coalition with M23</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/kabila-launches-new-coalition-with-m23</link><description>
In tonight's edition: DR Congo's former president Joseph Kabila has been named leader of a new rebel coalition, vowing to topple the Congolese government. Also, Africa's largest ever IPO has been extended. Plus Formula ⁠1 ⁠will return to ⁠Africa in ​the early 2030s, once a new circuit is built in Rwanda. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/91dc84b4-c743-11f1-8e7d-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b2a23995.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/91dc84b4-c743-11f1-8e7d-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b2a23995.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9ba84d4e-c742-11f1-98c2-ad6d31b61548</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:21:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clarisse FORTUNÉ</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>In Kenya, recycled plastic gets a second life as chess pieces</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/in-kenya-recycled-plastic-gets-a-second-life-as-chess-pieces</link><description>
In Nairobi, a project is helping children develop focus, patience and critical thinking through chess, using pieces made from recycled plastic waste.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a99973e-c718-11f1-9dfa-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-225312-225439-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a99973e-c718-11f1-9dfa-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-225312-225439-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4fa1c26a-c718-11f1-90b1-1b19ca1118fa</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:28:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>South Africa suspends asylum applications amid renewed anti-immigrant protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-amid-renewed-anti-immigrant-protests</link><description>
Tensions have flared in South Africa after a court ruling prompted the government to open its application system to all foreign nationals, regardless of their legal status. Despite applications remaining subject to approval, anti-immigrant protests erupted outside several Home Affairs offices, forcing authorities to temporarily suspend refugee and asylum applications. FRANCE 24's Eunice Masson has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e81674a6-c717-11f1-bdd1-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-224920-225113-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e81674a6-c717-11f1-bdd1-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-224920-225113-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eda485a2-c717-11f1-97e6-5f5703cb1bba</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:15:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ethiopian forces enter key Tigray town, raising fears among residents</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-forces-enter-key-tigray-town-raising-fears-among-residents</link><description>
Ethiopian federal forces and their allies have entered a key town in northern Tigray near the Eritrean border after rebel fighters withdrew. As the conflict intensifies, residents fear further violence and instability. Tom Canetti has the latest from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aeb1b5a4-c717-11f1-8351-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-224604-224800-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aeb1b5a4-c717-11f1-8351-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-224604-224800-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b3de80d4-c717-11f1-89b4-c75f6940fd2e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:13:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ethiopia: Social media becomes a battleground for propaganda</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-social-media-becomes-a-battleground-for-propaganda</link><description>
Millions of Ethiopians rely on social media for daily news. But as fighting resumes in the country’s north between federal forces and a coalition of rebel groups, these platforms have become a breeding ground for propaganda and disinformation. Pro-government and pro-rebel accounts are battling to shape the news, while journalists’ limited access to the front lines makes it increasingly difficult to verify what is happening on the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e1741d2-c6ea-11f1-a53e-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-081551-081737-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e1741d2-c6ea-11f1-a53e-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-081551-081737-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">592b129c-c6ea-11f1-9d63-c58701cbbe0f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:00:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tunisian duo Jathb blends Sufi traditions with electronic music</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tunisian-duo-jathb-blends-sufi-traditions-with-electronic-music</link><description>
Tunisian musical duo Jathb is reviving traditional Sufi chants by blending them with electronic beats and therapeutic sounds. After four years of gaining recognition both in Tunisia and internationally, the duo is also working to preserve the centuries-old Sufi music and texts that form part of the country’s cultural heritage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abdd228c-c6ea-11f1-85ba-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-081755-082016-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abdd228c-c6ea-11f1-85ba-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-081755-082016-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b13a327e-c6ea-11f1-b3ad-6ff3d044cbd6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:59:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>DR Congo’s former president Kabila to lead new movement with M23 rebels</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261012-dr-congo-former-president-joseph-kabila-to-lead-new-movement-with-m23-rebels</link><description>
 
 
Former DR Congo president Joseph Kabila announced a new political-military alliance with Rwanda-backed M23 rebels on Monday, despite being sentenced to death in absentia for alleged complicity with the group. The move comes as debate grows over constitutional changes ahead of President Felix Tshisekedi’s final term ending in 2028.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7910c4e6-7f90-11f0-99ca-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48NY9FH.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7910c4e6-7f90-11f0-99ca-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48NY9FH.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c1a5a36c-c683-11f1-bec4-a1ea1072ad80</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:27:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7910c4e6-7f90-11f0-99ca-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48NY9FH.jpg">© Jospin Mwisha, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Ethiopian government forces enter key Tigray town near Eritrea border</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-govt-forces-enter-key-tigray-town-near-eritrea-border</link><description>
In tonight's edition: Ethiopian forces tighten their grip on Tigray, advancing into the key town of Adwa after rebels withdrew. Also, police arrest 30 people amid violence across South Africa. Plus we head to Tunisia, where ancient Sufi chants collide with pulsating electronic beats.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2fb401d6-c6ee-11f1-8995-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-18873641116ace035ca209d6-61883076.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2fb401d6-c6ee-11f1-8995-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-18873641116ace035ca209d6-61883076.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0368a950-c67c-11f1-b90f-e322dce06a8f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:34:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jean-Emile JAMMINE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>At least 139 migrants die in boat wreck between Djibouti and Yemen</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/at-least-139-migrants-die-in-boat-wreck-between-djibouti-and-yemen</link><description>
At least 139 migrants died, including 15 children and 84 went missing when an overcrowded boat sank on its way from Djibouti to Yemen on the night between October 8 and 9. The International Organization for Migration said most of the people were Ethiopian when the vessel capsized off north of the town of Obock. Details by Morgan Ayre.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1dcbd28-c623-11f1-80e9-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-083759-083927-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1dcbd28-c623-11f1-80e9-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-083759-083927-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f6bb8202-c623-11f1-91f2-e9bc5d89a6fc</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:24:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Scores of gold miners killed in air strikes on Egypt-Sudan border, rights group says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261012-egypt-sudan-border-airstrikes-gold-miners-killed</link><description>
At least 72 workers were killed in air strikes on a gold mine on the Sudan-Egypt border on Saturday, a Sudanese rights group said on Sunday. The Emergency Lawyers organisation accused Egypt’s air force of the attack. AFP could not independently verify the account and Egypt has issued no official comment.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed29f7ca-c5db-11f1-8dcf-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP16118579529500.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed29f7ca-c5db-11f1-8dcf-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP16118579529500.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">32cf1d00-c5dc-11f1-91f7-9d438446f071</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:28:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed29f7ca-c5db-11f1-8dcf-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP16118579529500.jpg">© Brian Rohan, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
